          "position": "Capital Project Manager",
          "location": "Taipei, Taiwan",
          "period": "Sep 2022 - Dec 2023",
          "website": { "url": "", "label": "" },
          "description": "<ul><li><strong>Owner's Representative</strong> for a <strong>€12M fine chemical facility</strong> in Taiwan — state-of-the-art production line supplying specialty chemicals to TSMC advanced-node processes.</li><li>Managed cross-national, cross-functional teams within Merck's global matrix organization (Level-UP capital program).</li><li>Led FEED studies to establish technical scope, cost baseline, and execution roadmap; prepared financial analysis for the <strong>Global Capital Investment Committee's Final Investment Decision (FID)</strong>.</li><li>Oversaw construction and occupancy permitting; managed environmental assessments for air emission and wastewater discharge permits.</li><li>Independently developed and delivered a <strong>€3.5M skid-mounted high-purity specialty chemical production and supply system</strong> for TSMC advanced-node materials — from R&amp;D concept through detailed design, procurement, construction, and on-stream commissioning.</li><li><strong>Nominated for Merck Taiwan Q-Star Award (2023)</strong> for high-impact innovation in state-of-the-art process delivery.</li></ul>"
        },
